Updates the AI model to `openai/gpt-5` (multimodal) and enables relaunching analysis when API calls fail without requiring re-recording. Also adds audio download functionality and customizable model name configuration. **All recordings use WAV format exclusively - no WebM support.**

## Changes

- **Model**: Updated from `gpt-4o-audio-preview` to `openai/gpt-5`
- **Retry functionality**: 
  - Store recorded audio blob in `lastAudioBlob` variable
  - Display "🔄 Relancer l'analyse" button in error messages
  - Add `retryAnalysis()` function to reprocess stored audio
- **Audio Format** (WAV/MP3 only - **NO WebM**): 
  - Recording uses **WAV format exclusively** (no WebM fallback)
  - Shows error if browser doesn't support WAV recording
  - Downloads as `.wav` or `.mp3` file with timestamp based on actual format
  - Dynamic file extension: `enregistrement-YYYY-MM-DD...{wav|mp3}`
  - Button enabled after recording completion
- **Customizable Model Name**:
  - Added "Nom du modèle" input field in configuration section
  - Default value: `openai/gpt-5`
  - Saved to localStorage for persistence
  - Supports URL parameter: `?model=your-model-name`
  - Model name used dynamically in API calls
- **API Structure**: 
  - Added `modalities: ["text"]` field
  - Restructured to match OpenAI audio API format
  - Single user message with text + audio content array
  - Removed system message (combined into user text)
  - Dynamic audio format detection (`wav` or `mp3` only)
- **Documentation**: Updated README with new features and usage instructions

## Implementation

```javascript
// Recording with WAV only - NO WebM support
if (!MediaRecorder.isTypeSupported('audio/wav')) {
    throw new Error('Votre navigateur ne supporte pas l\'enregistrement audio WAV. Veuillez utiliser un navigateur compatible.');
}
const mimeType = 'audio/wav';
mediaRecorder = new MediaRecorder(stream, { mimeType });

// Store audio for retry and download
mediaRecorder.onstop = async () => {
    const audioBlob = new Blob(audioChunks, { type: mimeType });
    lastAudioBlob = audioBlob;
    downloadBtn.disabled = false;
    await processRecording(audioBlob);
};

// Download with WAV/MP3 only
let extension = 'wav';
if (lastAudioBlob.type.includes('mp3')) {
    extension = 'mp3';
}
a.download = `enregistrement-${timestamp}.${extension}`;

// API payload structure (matches OpenAI format)
{
    model: modelName,
    modalities: ["text"],
    messages: [
        {
            role: "user",
            content: [
                { type: "text", text: "...instructions..." },
                {
                    type: "input_audio",
                    input_audio: {
                        data: audioBase64.split(',')[1],
                        format: audioFormat  // 'wav' or 'mp3' only
                    }
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}

// Retry without re-recording
async function retryAnalysis() {
    if (lastAudioBlob) {
        await processRecording(lastAudioBlob);
    }
}
```

Error messages now include a retry button that reuses the last recording, handling transient failures (network issues, rate limits) without user intervention beyond a single click.

**Important**: WebM format is completely removed from the application. Only WAV and MP3 formats are supported. Browsers that don't support WAV recording will display an error message.

